# The epilogue week at every leader (docs/EPILOGUE.md, "Carriers"; docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The last week").
# Lines read four separate things and never mix them up: the world's outcome (cure_held, ending), who
# was there (was), this player's route (route), and this character's memory. "The cure." gives the
# leader's own read and opens the built carriers (the season at this seat, where to look); "Me." is
# the leader on themselves, a week from the barrier. Nothing here pays anything.
# Spoken straight to the player; the barriers stay closed until processing, then the north road.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ The Haven
conv epilogue.haven.cure
for leader:haven
when epilogue
topic "What's happening with the cure?"
prio world
voice haven

node start
  say? cure_held:haven :: It went hand to hand, house to house, like we always said it would. The houses argued about who went first. They're still arguing. That's how you know it's ours.
  say? cure_held:bastion :: Bastion has it in crates with numbers on, and it's issued by name and signature. We're on their list. Everyone's on a list now, even us.
  say? cure_held:redhand :: The Red Hand has it, and there's a price on a board at the crossroads. We're paying in tins. They're keeping the tins, mostly.
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: The lab published it. Every name on the paper, the volunteers too, by number. I read it twice. I understood it the second time.
  say? cure_held:everyone :: Somebody walked it out to every house. No crate, no list, no price. Nobody would say who to thank, so we thank everyone at supper.
  say It came. That's the part I keep saying out loud, to see if it's true. The line's stood down. The barriers stay shut until processing, then it's the north road, one name at a time.
  > @here What happened here, this season? -> season
  > @look Where should I go before it's over? -> look
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node season
  say Sit down. I'll tell it the way the house tells it, names and all.
  do call:season
  > @back2 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node look
  say Places you haven't been yet, and people who'd like to see you before the north road. I'll name them, and you go.
  do call:look
  > @back3 I'll go. Something else. -> hub

conv epilogue.haven.me
for leader:haven
when epilogue
topic "What will you do now?"
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say? route:won :: You stood with us at the end, when it mattered. I won't forget it, and nobody in this house will let me.
  say? route:lost :: You picked someone else's way for the cure. You'll still be fed here. We've fed people who picked worse.
  say? was:every_name :: You were at the table when the names were read. I saw you. I saw who you looked at.
  say When they open the north road I'll be the last one out of this house. Somebody has to count the stores one more time and lock the door, and leave the bear on it.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Bastion
conv epilogue.bastion.cure
for leader:bastion
when epilogue
topic "What's happening with the cure?"
prio world
voice bastion

node start
  say? cure_held:bastion :: We hold it. Issued against name and signature, at the north road and at the posts. In order. As planned, for once.
  say? cure_held:haven :: The Haven hands it out at its houses, with no register. Somebody has to keep one, so we do, from what people tell us at the wire.
  say? cure_held:redhand :: The Red Hand sells it, at a price on a board. Logged as theft. The log doesn't help anyone, but it's accurate.
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: Published. The lab put every name on the paper but ours. Noted.
  say? cure_held:everyone :: Carried out to everyone by persons unknown. Unregistered. I've stopped writing to Command about it, and Command has stopped not answering.
  say Cure confirmed. The line's stood down: no drones, no snipers. Processing at the road checkpoints. The order hasn't changed. The tone has.
  > @here What happened here, this season? -> season
  > @look Where should I go before it's over? -> look
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node season
  say For the log, then. Names, dates, what we held and what we didn't.
  do call:season
  > @back2 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node look
  say Grid squares you haven't covered, and people you haven't reported to. Cover them before processing.
  do call:look
  > @back3 I'll cover them. Something else. -> hub

conv epilogue.bastion.me
for leader:bastion
when epilogue
topic "What will you do now?"
prio flavour
voice bastion

node start
  say? route:won :: You signed on with us for the cure and held to it. That goes in the log, in ink.
  say? route:lost :: You signed for someone else's route. Logged. Now eat something.
  say? was:orders :: You were there when the orders were read. You'll remember them longer than Command did.
  say Hand over the post. Sign for the stores. Read the roll one last time, all of it. Then walk out last at the north road. Same as any posting.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ The Red Hand
conv epilogue.redhand.cure
for leader:redhand
when epilogue
topic "What's happening with the cure?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say? cure_held:redhand :: Ours. Priced fair. Fair to us. The queue's at the board at the crossroads, and the board's got prices on it.
  say? cure_held:bastion :: Bastion's got it in crates. We've got the crates' address. Patience.
  say? cure_held:haven :: The Haven's giving it away. Free! Terrible for business. Good for everyone else, I'm told.
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: The beaks printed the recipe. You can't sell a recipe everyone's read. I've tried.
  say? cure_held:everyone :: Somebody gave it to everyone for nothing. I've been robbed before, but never on behalf of the whole Zone.
  say It's out. The drones have gone home. Everything's for sale again, including leaving, and leaving's the one thing I can't put a price on yet.
  > @here What happened here, this season? -> season
  > @look Where should I go before it's over? -> look
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node season
  say The book remembers everything. Sit. I'll read you the good bits.
  do call:season
  > @back2 Thanks. Something else. -> hub

node look
  say Places you haven't robbed yet. That's a joke. Half of one. Here's where.
  do call:look
  > @back3 I'll go. Something else. -> hub

conv epilogue.redhand.me
for leader:redhand
when epilogue
topic "What will you do now?"
prio flavour
voice redhand

node start
  say? route:won :: You stood with the book for the cure. The book stands with you. That's as warm as it gets round here.
  say? route:lost :: You backed the other horse. No hard feelings. A few soft ones.
  say? was:book :: You were at the table when the book was closed. You know what's in it. That makes two of us.
  say Me? Close the book. Count it twice. Then walk up the north road and see what the outside charges for a sandwich.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Halcyon
conv epilogue.halcyon.cure
for leader:halcyon
when epilogue
topic "What's happening with the cure?"
prio world
voice halcyon

node start
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: Published. Every author named, the volunteers by number. The method is pinned to the lab door. Someone corrected the spelling.
  say? cure_held:bastion :: Bastion holds the stock. They issue it alphabetically. We're under H.
  say? cure_held:haven :: The Haven distributes it by hand. Unmeasured. Effective, by every measure we have.
  say? cure_held:redhand :: Sold. The dose is ours. The price is theirs. We've recorded both.
  say? cure_held:everyone :: Distributed without control or record. The outcome is good. We're revising our assumptions.
  say The work is done. The line has stood down, and processing starts at the road checkpoints. The record is not done. It never is.
  > @here What happened here, this season? -> season
  > @look Where should I go before it's over? -> look
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node season
  say The record, then. The short version, with dates.
  do call:season
  > @back2 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node look
  say Unsampled locations. Your notebook should list them. It probably doesn't, so I will.
  do call:look
  > @back3 I'll go. Something else. -> hub

conv epilogue.halcyon.me
for leader:halcyon
when epilogue
topic "What will you do now?"
prio flavour
voice halcyon

node start
  say? route:won :: You chose the paper. Your name is in the acknowledgements. Small type. Still there.
  say? route:lost :: You chose another route. That is also data.
  say? was:proof :: You were there when the paper went out. Witness noted.
  say Write it up. Every page, including the first one, which nobody wants to write. Then leave by the north road, in the queue, like anyone.
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub
